  "design": {
    "entrance": "Studio strip lights clunk on one by one; the chrome title, lying back on the glossy floor, pivots upright on its base (X rotation 78 deg to 0) toward a low-angle camera.",
    "reveal": "At the lock the strip-light reflections race across the chrome faces, a cold edge light snaps on and the floor mirror catches the full title.",
    "camera": "Low-angle dolly-in that rises slightly to eye level; compact shake at the lock.",
    "material": "Mirror chrome: near-zero diffuse, very high specular exponent, layered strip reflections over a black horizon band, crisp bevels with cool edge illumination, dark extruded walls.",
    "exit": "The title falls back flat into the floor reflection while the strip lights switch off in reverse order."
  },
  "fusion_notes": [
    "Approximation: the Fusion MtlBlinn cannot reflect an environment, so the chrome look is built from a very high specular exponent, three animated spot/directional highlights and screen-space strip reflections (masked light sweeps). For true mirror chrome, replace GoldMtl-style Blinn ('ChromeMtl') with a MtlReflect fed by an HDRI SphereMap - not generated because those tool IDs are unverified here.",
    "The floor reflection is a flipped 2D copy of the rendered title (Transform FlipVert), not a ray-traced mirror; it stays correct while the title is upright and is faded out during the fall-back exit."
  ],
